			"Message": "build(deps-dev): bump @vitest/coverage-v8 from 4.1.2 to 4.1.3\n\nBumps [@vitest/coverage-v8](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/tree/HEAD/packages/coverage-v8) from 4.1.2 to 4.1.3.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/commits/v4.1.3/packages/coverage-v8)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@vitest/coverage-v8\"\n  dependency-version: 4.1.3\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "525f2a841ff1a88bc3006f879b8f5d744148e866"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-06T10:17:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				276,
				9
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Replace hand-written shims with real VS Code types from @codeeditorland/output\n\nCentralize all VS Code type constructors in a single Platform/VSCode/Type barrel that re-exports compiled types from @codeeditorland/output:\n- extHostTypes: Position, Range, Location, Selection, MarkdownString, Hover, CompletionItem, Diagnostic, TextEdit, WorkspaceEdit, etc.\n- uri.js: URI class (exposed as Uri)\n- cancellation.js: CancellationToken, CancellationTokenSource\n- event.js: Emitter (vscode.EventEmitter equivalent)\n\nReplace hand-written shims across the codebase:\n- Handler.ts: Remove CancellationTokenSource class, import from @codeeditorland/output\n- TypeConverter.ts: Use real URI.parse instead of vscode Uri type\n- GRPCServerService.ts: Use real Position/Range classes instead of MakePosition/MakeRange shims; real CancellationTokenSource instead of stub\n- ViewColumn.ts: Import from @codeeditorland/output\n- TreeView/Item.ts: Import TreeItemCollapsibleState from Platform/VSCode/Type barrel\n- APIFactoryService.ts: Expose 40+ type constructors on the vscode API for extensions\n- Window.ts: Switch to type-only import\n\nThis eliminates duplicate shim implementations scattered across multiple files, ensuring all extensions use the same VS Code class definitions. The single source of truth in Platform/VSCode/Type.ts makes updates straightforward when the Output package changes.",
			"SHA": "b586550d56b96eb328d356841bf35393f7d3df90"
		},
